{"availability":"available","full":"maximilianfeix/proxy-scraper","name":"proxy-scraper","description":"Free HTTP/SOCKS proxies with every check on the record: passed, failed or couldn't run, and when. Hourly list, --pick --verify, --diagnose, rotating proxy, Python API, MCP server.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":52,"forks":10,"created":"2026-09-24T12:33:28Z","updated":"2026-10-17T06:49:27Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://maximilianfeix.github.io/proxy-scraper/","topics":["ai-agents","cli","discord-bot","free-proxy","hacktoberfest","http-proxy","mcp","mcp-server","proxy","proxy-checker","proxy-list","proxy-scraper","proxy-server","python","rotating-proxy","scraper","socks4","socks5","web-scraping"],"demo":"https://maximilianfeix.github.io/proxy-scraper/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T07:10:08.159Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T07:10:08.159Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T07:10:08.159Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.276Z","stars":46,"forks":10},{"at":"2026-10-17T07:10:08.159Z","stars":52,"forks":10}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["[]( []( [](#live-list) []( []( [](pyproject.toml) []( [](LICENSE)","Most free proxy lists are 95 % dead, and a good part of the rest are honeypots or proxies that inject scripts into your pages. proxy-scraper collects public HTTP, SOCKS4 and SOCKS5 proxies from 700+ sources and keeps only the ones that pass every check. It learns with every run which sources are worth it, and it can turn the result into a single rotating proxy.","In numbers: in one day it checked 3.6 million free proxies – 1.1 % worked, and more than half of the ones that answered failed a second request. What's actually out there →"],"features":["Features · Why not just download a list?","Rotating proxy server","Discord and Telegram bot","Started without arguments, the tool asks what you need using the arrow keys – a preset or step by step. At the end it shows the matching command line.","700+ sources fetched in parallel, large lists parsed on all CPU cores, hand-written HTTP/SOCKS handshakes directly on asyncio with 2000+ checks at once."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/maximilianfeix/proxy-scraper/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9e0a19ec612ac477925f445a358fd342c0194af8a1e81d7d861386c1485361fc","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.336Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.336Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"[]( []( [](#live-list) []( []( [](pyproject.toml) []( [](LICENSE)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/maximilianfeix/proxy-scraper/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Username wishes – country-us sends everything out through US proxies, session-NAME keeps one exit IP for a login flow – reach the server as the proxy login. mitmproxy sends it right away; Burp and ZAP may wait to be asked, so start the server with --serve-password when you rely on a wish there.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/maximilianfeix/proxy-scraper/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Lines like socks5://user:pass@1.2.3.4:1080 keep their login: HTTP proxies get a Proxy-Authorization header, SOCKS5 uses username/password auth (RFC 1929), SOCKS4 the user ID.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/maximilianfeix/proxy-scraper/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"9e0a19ec612ac477925f445a358fd342c0194af8a1e81d7d861386c1485361fc","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/maximilianfeix/proxy-scraper/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.337Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T06:52:52Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/maximilianfeix/proxy-scraper/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:18.340Z","hash":"9e0a19ec612ac477925f445a358fd342c0194af8a1e81d7d861386c1485361fc","originalBytes":63054,"storedBytes":63054,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026